# REPRODUCIBILITY — measured, not assumed. Do not upgrade this claim without
# re-measuring.
#
# liblogoschat.so is NOT bit-for-bit reproducible today. Measured on the 6dd23bc7…
# build — the non-determinism is toolchain-side, so it carries to 6b12a4fb… and
# 84b751c2…, and it has NOT been re-measured on either. A full `cargo clean` and
# rerun of scripts/build-android-arm64.sh on the SAME host, same source, same build
# path yielded 812230801e01c051925e844368951c58e786efbbd8f192c548b2ae0e7a97273f
# instead of 6dd23bc7…: identical byte size, identical exported-symbol set, and the
# only differing STRING is an AWS-LC build stamp — `built on: <UTC date>`, emitted by
# the aws-lc-rs/aws-lc-sys cmake build — with ~136 KB of .rodata/.text/.rela.dyn
# layout churn behind it.
#
# So "re-derive the hash from source" is not available at this revision, and
# publishing the exact artifact (above) is the only sound provenance we have.
# Removing that timestamp stamp and proving determinism is tracked under #366.
#
# Beware the trap this measurement caught: a rebuild with a WARM cargo cache
# (`cargo clean -p` of only the changed crates) does reproduce 6dd23bc7… exactly,
# because the stamped aws-lc objects are reused. That result looks like proof of
# reproducibility and is not. Only a full clean rebuild answers the question.
